# .env.local is WRITTEN BY THE NEON CLI — you normally never create it by hand:
#   npx neon@latest login      (once per machine)
#   npx neon env pull          (or `neon deploy` / `neon checkout <branch>`, which pull too)
# That writes the pinned branch's variables (see .neon for the link):
#   DATABASE_URL              pooled endpoint (-pooler) — what the app uses
#   DATABASE_URL_UNPOOLED     direct endpoint — what drizzle-kit migrations use
#   NEON_BRANCH, NEON_BRANCH_ID, NEON_FUNCTION_HOST_SUFFIX
# Only Next.js auto-loads .env.local; the db:* scripts load it through dotenv-cli.
#
# Manual fallback (no Neon CLI): paste the two connection strings from the Neon console.
DATABASE_URL=
DATABASE_URL_UNPOOLED=
